I'm putting together a FAQ file for civil liberties issues, which
would be a FAQ for alt.society.civil-liberty.  I'm also putting
together some other documents / pointers to documents, ftp archives
etc. on a gopher server.  (see comp.infosystems.gopher FAQ for more
information on using gopher).

Here is the gopher directory from otax.tky.hut.fi, Topics/Civil-liberties:

    1. Alt.drugs FAQ archive at milton.u.washington.edu/
    2. Civil liberties FTP archive at ftp.eff.org/
    3. FTP archive at ftp.eff.org/
    4. Overview
    5. Subtopics
    6. US Constitution, activism material, pit-manager.mit.edu/
    7. US Government-related docs, Senate fax#, etc., ftp.eff.org/
    8. US Libertarian Party, FIJA, libernet@think.com/

Here's the Overview document:

Author: Jyrki Kuoppala (jkp@cs.hut.fi)
Last modified: Tue Sep  1 05:37:18 1992


FTP archives:

Electronic Frontier Foundation

ftp.eff.org  /pub



Gopher servers:

Helsinki University of Techology/Student Body

otax.tky.hut.fi, port 70, Topics/Civil-liberties



Usenet newsgroups:

alt.society.civil-liberty

Reports and discussions on civil liberties


alt.censorship

Talk on censorship


alt.privacy,comp.society.privacy(moderated)

Privacy issues


alt.comp.acad-freedom.news(moderated)/talk

News and discussions on academic freedom on electronic media.  Carl
Kadie posts excellent references on civil liberties issues on these
groups, with pointers to electronic versions of the material (Supreme
Court decisions, various policies, etc.) available on the net.


comp.org.eff.news(moderated)/talk

News from the Electronic Frontier Foundation, an organization working
for civil liberties on the electronic frontier, and discussions about
the electronic frontier.


misc.activism.progressive(moderated)

Sometimes has reports on civil liberties violations and often news
relevant to civil liberties


alt.activism/alt.activism.d

Sometimes has reports on civil liberties violations and news relevant
to civil liberties, but currently mostly appears to be a somewhat less
"mainstream" replica of talk.politics.misc.


alt.drugs,talk.politics.drugs

Apparently because of the "War on Drugs" in USA and hysteria about
drugs in many places on the world, alt.drugs and talk.politics.drugs
discuss many civil liberties issues


soc.culture.usa

Despite flames, a dimwit alien non-Usonian posts articles discussing
civil liberties to this newsgroup having the bizarre idea that the
Land of the Free and Home of the Brave is currently not what it
claims, and thus the group has some civil liberties traffic.  Well,
the topic does pop up often by other posters, too.


soc.rights.human

Human rights


sci.crypt

Occasional discussions on the cryptography export restrictions in USA.


comp.risks

Occasionally has articles connected with civil-liberties.


comp.society.cu-digest

The Computer Underground Digest, news and articles from the electronic
frontier.


misc.legal

The official legal view of U.S. Constitution is available here, with
occasional dissent from people who have bizarre ideas like that the
U.S. Constitution is interpreted with common sense by the Supreme
Court, that "Congress shall make no law abridging the freedom of
speech" means that also laws against publishing sexually explicit
material are unconstitional, or that since the alcohol prohibition was
passed by a constitutional amendment prohibition on other drugs is
unconstitutional because there's no amendment prohibiting them.



